Pursuant to 15 U.S.C. 1681c-2 ( the Fair Credit Reporting Act ), the CRAs are required to block the reporting of fraudulent information resulting from identity theft within four business days of receiving proof of the identity theft, a copy of the identity theft report, and an identification of the fraudulent items to be blocked. Despite meeting these requirements and making multiple requests, the credit reporting agencies have failed to comply with this legal obligation. 

The failure to remove this fraudulent information is not a matter of negligence or oversight but constitutes willful non-compliance with the FCRA. This deliberate disregard for federal law has caused significant and ongoing harm to consumers credit standing, financial well-being, and peace of mind. 

Under 15 U.S.C. 1681n, consumer is entitled to seek damages for this willful violation, including actual damages, statutory damages, punitive damages, and reasonable attorneys fees and costs.

Consumer has contacted the credit reporting agencies XXXX, XXXX and Equifax and provided all required information, yet the fraudulent items remain on consumers credit file. This failure to act is causing continued harm to consumers credit score and financial well-being. 

Consumer is requesting that the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau intervene to ensure that the credit reporting agencies immediately comply with the law, remove all fraudulent information from consumers credit report and credit file, and prevent further damage to consumers credit standing. 

Requested Resolution : 1. Immediate removal of all fraudulent information from consumer credit report, in accordance with 15 U.S.C. 1681c-2.

2. Confirmation in writing that the fraudulent information has been removed.

3. An investigation into the credit reporting agencies non-compliance with federal law.

Remedy for non compliance of {$5000.00} pee 15 usc 1681n! Through electronic funds transfer. 
