It is important to note that SMS verification, while commonly used, can be vulnerable to various forms of attacks and fraud, particularly when a device has been compromised. SMS messages can be intercepted, spoofed, or manipulated by attackers, especially in cases of SIM swapping, device theft, or phishing attacks. This makes SMS an unreliable method of verification in situations where a customers phone has been compromised. 

Given these vulnerabilities, it is not reasonable to rely solely on SMS verification as a basis for denying my fraud claim. The fact that these unauthorized charges were approved through an SMS message on a stolen phone should not be held against me. I have never conducted business with the merchant in question, and I did not authorize these transactions. 

