Violation of the Privacy Act of 1974 Furthermore, these disclosures also contravene the Privacy Act of 1974, which protects personal and financial data from unauthorized sharing without consent. In this case, my transaction history contains sensitive personal information, and I have not authorized Capital One Bank or XXXX XXXX Bank to disclose these details to any third-party, including credit reporting agencies. Therefore, I believe both financial institutions are in violation of the Privacy Act for improperly handling my private financial information. 
